('advanced-native-1659', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1659-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["喬以記分比喻反思累積經歷與自身疲倦。"],"options":["喬以記分比喻反思累積經歷與自身疲倦。","喬報告醫護人員已確認她疲倦的確切原因。","喬認為那些深夜工作與她現在的感受沒有關係。","喬說自己只累了一分鐘，與先前數周經歷無關。"]},"advanced-native-1659-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["She is looking back at how the repeated experience seemed to affect her.","By saying the body eventually keeps score, she reflects on the tiredness that followed those weeks.","She connects her present fatigue with a longer pattern of late-night work.","The image gives a personal sense of accumulated effects rather than a literal number."],"options":["She is looking back at how the repeated experience seemed to affect her.","By saying the body eventually keeps score, she reflects on the tiredness that followed those weeks.","She connects her present fatigue with a longer pattern of late-night work.","The image gives a personal sense of accumulated effects rather than a literal number."]},"advanced-native-1659-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["At the reunion, he felt the body eventually keeps score after the repeated rehearsals and journeys."],"options":["At the reunion, he felt the body eventually keeps score after the repeated rehearsals and journeys.","He left early because he had lost interest in meeting his family, rather than because he felt tired.","His reflection concerns only that day’s long lunch, with the earlier travel left out of the account."]},"advanced-native-1659-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["這句比喻本身可確定某個人的病因及結果。"],"options":["這句比喻本身可確定某個人的病因及結果。","仍需具體資料，才能了解某次經歷造成甚麼影響。","說話者在用累積記錄的意象談身體經驗。"]},"advanced-native-1659-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["It is a metaphor for accumulated effects in her account, not a reported medical score."],"options":["Describe the fatigue as a one-off reaction and leave the repeated late nights out of the interpretation.","It is a metaphor for accumulated effects in her account, not a reported medical score.","Treat the image as